# Change report

After fast iteration and the drift review (`references/triage-and-iteration.md`), the owner reviews what changed in one page: every anchor and plan item changed in the round, with its scores before and after. `scripts/change_report.py` builds it from local files, git and the tracker; it never calls Jev.

## Run it

```bash
R="<this skill's directory>/scripts/change_report.py"
python3 "$R" --anchors "$A" --baseline-rev <commit before the round> \
  --fixture-checks <check-fixtures output, oldest first> ... \
  --tuning-result <tournament result_vars.json, oldest first> ... \
  --drift-file "$P/anchor-tuning/drift-review-<date>.json" \
  --out "$P/reports" --name <phase>-changes
```

| Flag | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `--anchors` | `anchors.json` now; the baseline is the same file at `--baseline-rev` (`git show`) |
| `--baseline-rev` | the commit holding `anchors.json` before the round |
| `--plan-dir` | the plan folder holding `anchor-runs/` (default: the folder holding `--anchors`) |
| `--gate` | `plan` (default) or `dev`: which runs to read; dry and fixture runs are skipped |
| `--item` | limit to these items (repeatable); default every item with a run |
| `--fixture-checks` | `check-fixtures` JSON outputs, oldest first; per anchor the first file holding it is "before", the last "after" |
| `--tuning-result` | each tournament's `result_vars.json`, oldest first; "default" is the first tournament's `baseline_exact` cases, "tuned" the last accepted one's `semantic_score.stable_cases` |
| `--drift-file` | the drift review JSON (`assets/schemas/drift-review.schema.json`); optional |
| `--out`, `--name` | writes `<out>/<name>.html`, the JSON sidecar `<out>/<name>.json` and one XHTML panel per unit in `<out>/<name>/` (default name `change-report`) |
| `--title` | page title |
| `--repository-root` | where `.sc/plan-anchor/settings.yaml` is looked up (default `.`) |

Output is the JSON envelope `{success, data, error}`: `data` names the page, sidecar and panels, the overall `status` and any `warnings` (an item with no run, an item whose earlier text was not found). Exit 0 when the report was written; 2 with a typed error: `VALIDATION.INPUT`, `SCRIPT.IO`, `GIT.BASELINE` (not a git repository, or the revision does not hold the file), `DRIFT.INVALID` (`data.problems` lists every schema violation), `DEPENDENCY.SC_COMPOSE`, `RENDER.FAILED`, `SETTINGS.*`, `SCRIPT.INTERNAL`; 130 on interrupt.

## What it shows

- **Plan items.** Per item, the first and the last run: pass or fail, satisfied / applicable anchors (not-applicable and excluded anchors left out), the failing anchors, every run, and each exclusion with its reason. The text diff runs from the version the first run judged to now: {% if tracker == "bd" %}for a `bd` issue, the `bd history` entry at or before the first run against `bd show`{% elif tracker == "br" %}for a `br` issue, the `.beads/issues.jsonl` committed at or before the first run against `br show` (only committed versions are known){% endif %}, field by field (`title`, `description`, `acceptance_criteria`, `design`); for a Markdown plan item, the run's item file as committed at or before the first run against the file now.
- **Anchors.** Every anchor locked at the baseline or now, plus any whose record changed: word diffs of statement, scope, status, kind, quote, deterministic check and fixtures; history events since the baseline (a retirement and its reason); exclusions with reasons, marked added, kept or removed; fixture checks before and after; default and tuned question scores.
- **Drift review.** Findings as a table (severity, location, what changed, authority and its quote, suggested fix, status and fix note), the acceptable choices and the confirmations.
- The page status is `FAIL` when an item's last run fails, else `DRIFT` while a finding is `open`, else `PASS`.

Each panel has Copy JSON and Copy Context buttons; the page has a table of contents, status pills and a dark mode. Tracker ids (items and anchor beads) are links when `issue_url_template` is set in `.sc/plan-anchor/settings.yaml` (`python3 "<this skill's directory>/scripts/plan_anchor_settings.py" set issue_url_template 'https://tracker.example/issues/{id}'`), plain text otherwise.

## How it renders

Two templates, as the sc-compose html-report pattern prescribes: each panel is one strict, render-checked `sc-compose render` of `templates/sprint-panel.xhtml.j2`, `templates/anchor-panel.xhtml.j2` or `templates/drift-panel.xhtml.j2`; the page is one render of `templates/change-report.html.j2`, which receives only top-level arrays and the rendered panels. The script assembles no HTML except the word-diff fragments (escaped text inside `<del>` and `<ins>`). The sidecar holds the whole data model, item texts included.

Showing the user the page is mandatory: the round is not finished until they have it. Send the page and say where the sidecar is. In the same message, list in prose every ADR, REQ, NFR and ANC change by id with what changed, or say there are none. Commit both beside the plan with the drift review JSON when the plan is committed.
